/i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas21.jpg?resize=320%2C469&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas21.jpg?resize=768%2C1125&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas21.jpg?resize=600%2C879&amp;ssl=1 600w\" /></a><figcaption><em>Opisthoteuthis</em> Verrill. Available <a href=\"https://society6.com/product/art-by-friedrich-wilhelm-winter-from-cephalopod-atlas-by-carl-chun-1910-benefitting-greenpeace2663654_print?sku=s6-13477937p4a1v1?curator=brainpicker\" target=\"_blank\">as a print</a>.</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://society6.com/product/art-by-friedrich-wilhelm-winter-from-cephalopod-atlas-by-carl-chun-1910-benefitting-greenpeace2663655_print?sku=s6-13477940p4a1v1?curator=brainpicker\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas22.jpg?resize=680%2C996&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"996\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas22.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas22.jpg?resize=240%2C352&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas22.jpg?resize=320%2C469&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas22.jpg?resize=768%2C1125&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas22.jpg?resize=600%2C879&amp;ssl=1 600w\" /></a><figcaption><em>Opisthoteuthis</em> Verrill. Available <a href=\"https://society6.com/product/art-by-friedrich-wilhelm-winter-from-cephalopod-atlas-by-carl-chun-1910-benefitting-greenpeace2663655_print?sku=s6-13477940p4a1v1?curator=brainpicker\" target=\"_blank\">as a print</a>.</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://society6.com/product/art-by-friedrich-wilhelm-winter-from-cephalopod-atlas-by-carl-chun-1910-benefitting-greenpeace2663634_print?sku=s6-13477898p4a1v1?curator=brainpicker\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas10.jpg?resize=680%2C963&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"963\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas10.jpg?w=900&amp;ssl=1 900w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas10.jpg?resize=240%2C340&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas10.jpg?resize=320%2C453&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas10.jpg?resize=768%2C1088&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas10.jpg?resize=600%2C850&amp;ssl=1 600w\" /></a><figcaption><em>Benthoteuthis megalops</em> Verrill. Available <a href=\"https://society6.com/product/art-by-friedrich-wilhelm-winter-from-cephalopod-atlas-by-carl-chun-1910-benefitting-greenpeace2663634_print?sku=s6-13477898p4a1v1?curator=brainpicker\" target=\"_blank\">as a print</a>.</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><a href=\"https://society6.com/product/art-by-friedrich-wilhelm-winter-from-cephalopod-atlas-by-carl-chun-1910-benefitting-greenpeace2663648_print?sku=s6-13477926p4a1v1?curator=brainpicker\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas17.jpg?resize=680%2C996&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"996\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas17.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas17.jpg?resize=240%2C352&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas17.jpg?resize=320%2C469&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas17.jpg?resize=768%2C1125&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2020/03/CephalopodAtlas17.jpg?resize=600%2C879&amp;ssl=1 600w\" /></a><figcaption><em>Eledonella pygmaea</em> Verr. Available <a href=\"https://society6.com/product/art-by-friedrich-wilhelm-winter-from-cephalopod-atlas-by-carl-chun-1910-benefitting-greenpeace2663648_print?sku=s6-13477926p4a1v1?curator=brainpicker\" target=\"_blank\">as a print</a>.</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Complement with an animated primer on <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2016/02/15/ted-ed-octopus-consciousness/\">what makes the octopus consciousness so extraordinary</a> and a little boy’s <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2015/05/29/luiz-eating-animals-octopus/\">disarming case against eating octopuses</a> (I’ll take the PSA opportunity here to remind folks that “octopus” comes from Greek, not from Latin; the correct plural is therefore “octopuses,” not “octopi”), then revisit British artist Sarah Stone’s trailblazing <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2019/03/12/sarah-stone-natural-history-illustration/\">natural history paintings of exotic and endangered species</a> from the previous century, French artist Paul Sougy’s <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2019/11/29/paul-sougy/\">vintage scientific diagrams of plants and animals</a> from the following century, and Sy Montgomery’s lovely contemporary meditation on <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2018/10/31/how-to-be-a-good-creature-sy-montgomery/\">how to be a good creature</a>.</p>\n<hr /><h3>donating = loving</h3><p>For seventeen years, I have been spending hundreds of hours and thousands of dollars each month composing <em>The Marginalian</em> (which <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2021/10/22/brain-pickings-becoming-the-marginalian/\">bore the outgrown name <em>Brain Pickings</em></a> for its first fifteen years). It has remained free and ad-free and alive thanks to patronage from readers. I have no staff, no interns, no assistant — a thoroughly one-woman labor of love that is also my life and my livelihood. If this labor makes your own life more livable in any way, please consider lending a helping hand with a <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\">donation</a>. Your support makes all the difference.</p>\n\n<hr />\n\n<h3>newsletter</h3>\n<p><em>The Marginalian</em> has a free weekly newsletter. It comes out on Sundays and offers the week’s most inspiring reading. Here’s <a href=\"https://mailchi.mp/brainpickings/janna-levin-rebecca-elson-anne-lamott-james-gleick\">what to expect</a>. Like? <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/newsletter/\">Sign up.</a></p>","author":"Maria Popova","siteTitle":"The Marginalian","siteHash":"052ac1be0de11784b9ef27664fbcf33da8263d0e7cb9c6e601ccd959f2d3aa78","entryHash":"21d05bdc310636f16720b6fd7a57ab9381ad958ac074c8a1824c91e49137052b","category":"Sites"}